module test.claim.deployment_gate_answer_witness

// WITNESS FOR THE STAGE-2 ROUTE gunbc.fleet.deployment_gate_answer (the phase chain, ending in review_phase).
//
// WHAT THESE CLAIMS ARE OVER, STATED PLAINLY (DESIGN §3, "a witness discriminates at one interface").
// Every input below is a SUPPLIED WIRE FACT at the route's interface: the responses GitHub would return,
// the run record, the wait, the filed claim and the tapped capability. Nothing here performs HTTP, so
// no claim in this file establishes that a REAL transport produces those facts. That real-producer claim
// is the declared frontier recorded in gunbc.plans.ntfy_deployment_gate_approval ("Stage 2's declared
// frontier"): the route's consumer is the later actuator change, and the inhabitance claim becomes
// executable on the real I/O path when it lands.
//
// WHAT EACH CLAIM STILL EXECUTES: the REAL route. The honest-path claims drive the real confined mints
// (observe_gate_installation, observe_rule_ownership, admit_broker_answer, clear_review, review_request_of, mint_accepted_rule_review) through the chain, and
// the receipts they assert on can only have been built by the mint, so deleting the route's integration
// of the mints makes the inhabitance claims go red.
//
// THE REDS: forged binding, crossed run id, crossed environment, broker denied, dark state, and the two
// body-binding reds (a sent body for the sibling environment; a DENY proposal sent as Approved).
